// Double quotes inside a shell block keep their words together and expand the
// parameters they hold, each block read as written. Every block but the last
// stands before another root form, a stray refused where it stands; the last
// is a definition's body, which the lowering admits no shell block for yet
// (#1057).

/// A double-quoted argument with a space, a stray.
@[ refuses("OutOfFragment.WrongSort.declaration") ]
#!{ echo "hello world"; }

/// Escapes inside double quotes, a stray.
@[ refuses("OutOfFragment.WrongSort.declaration") ]
#!{ printf "col1\tcol2\n"; }

/// Parameters, bare and braced, expanded inside double quotes, a stray.
@[ refuses("OutOfFragment.WrongSort.declaration") ]
#!{ echo "home is $HOME and user is ${USER}"; }

/// A parameter inside a double-quoted argument beside a single-quoted format,
/// in a definition (#1057).
@[ refuses("OutOfFragment.shell_block") ]
def formatted() -> -F Unit { #!{ printf '%s\n' "value $x"; } }
